[PITCH] 1
  group-span.skool:119: states a pitch ('~1.3 kHz') — the #AUDIO plays the pitch, so the figure is the clip read back in numbers. Name what the sound means and what fires it; the tone formula belongs once at the primitive
    c$EC56 LD D,$64       ; The door-close click, ~1.3 kHz

[SPLICE] 1
  group-span.skool:110: this comment finishes the sentence the previous unit left open ('Hold the slot while the fade settles,') — each comment describes its own rows, so a clause that only makes sense after the one above it belongs in that one, or in a sentence of its own that names what it refers to
    *$EC4E LD A,(HL)      ; {and release it once the fade has passed.

